us 5.5 played F7, joining the stones on row 7, and lost 4.1 points; the engine's choice was H7. Black's lead went from -4.2 to -0.2, putting the game nearly level."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "Black F6 lost 4.2 points, taking Black's lead from +0.1 to -4.1, and the engine's choice was A5. White took A5 on the next move and lost only 0.1. After that the lead stayed near -4.0 through the end of the game, and White won by 4."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses the pasted board and prints each group's liberties, count.py only tallies stones and enclosed empty regions of the current position, and the games.md commands only read or append notes. None of them generates, scores or ranks candidate moves, or plays any continuation.", "stop": false}}